# name: test/sql/cityjson_wkb_ring_closing.test
# description: WKB rings are always closed, degenerate first==last rings included
# group: [sql]

require cityjson

# railway_appearance.city.jsonl object GMLID_855011_330784_753, lod 3, has two
# rings whose first and last vertex INDEX coincide: surface 67 ring [87, 71, 87] and
# surface 75 ring [87, 144, 88, 87]. CityJSON rings never repeat the first vertex.
# The four-index ring is a source ring explicitly closed: the repeat is stripped,
# leaving the triangle [87, 144, 88], which the WKB closes like any other ring (the
# same rule as cityparquet-rs's writer). The three-index ring cannot lose a vertex
# without becoming too short, so it stays a degenerate ring (an out-and-back edge,
# zero area), not an already-closed one -- it still needs its closing vertex
# appended. Skipping that emits a WKB ring that, once a strict reader strips the
# duplicate closing vertex, has too few points left to be a ring at all -- the root
# cause of cityparquet-rs's "polygon ring has 2 points after stripping the closing
# vertex, need at least 3" on this exact object.
#
# octet_length is a structural, byte-level check: the encoding with neither ring
# closed is 15678 bytes, and the degenerate ring gains one closing point (24 bytes:
# 3 doubles x 8 bytes), while the stripped ring gains its closing point in place of
# the repeat it lost.

query I
SELECT octet_length(geometry_lod3_0)
FROM read_cityjsonseq('test/data/railway_appearance.city.jsonl')
WHERE id = 'GMLID_855011_330784_753';
----
15702

# The closed geometry still round-trips through the WKB-parsing scalar
# functions without error, and its extent is unaffected by the added
# (duplicate) closing vertex.
query T
SELECT cityjson_wkb_geometry_type(geometry_lod3_0)
FROM read_cityjsonseq('test/data/railway_appearance.city.jsonl')
WHERE id = 'GMLID_855011_330784_753';
----
MultiPolygon Z

query I
SELECT cityjson_wkb_extent(geometry_lod3_0) IS NOT NULL
FROM read_cityjsonseq('test/data/railway_appearance.city.jsonl')
WHERE id = 'GMLID_855011_330784_753';
----
true
